.\" Man page for ax25tcpd.conf
.\"
.TH AX25TCPD.CONF 5 "11 Aug 2026" "ax25-apps" "Linux System Administration"
.SH NAME
ax25tcpd.conf \- configuration for ax25tcpd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ax25tcpd.conf
tells
.BR ax25tcpd (8)
where to find the AGWPE multiplexer it talks to (the back side) and
where it listens for its own clients (the front side).
.PP
Blank lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored.  A line consists of whitespace separated words.
.SH TARGET
The back side normally comes from the shared loop port configuration
.BR ax25common.conf (5),
the very file the
.BR ax25netd (8)
daemon reads for its listener: one file, one semantics.  The
.B loop socket
and
.B loop tcp
directives there decide how this frontend reaches the daemon.
.PP
For a netd on another host an explicit line overrides it:
.PP
.RS
.B target tcp
.I host tcp-port
.br
.B target socket
.I path
.RE
.PP
.B ax25tcpd
opens a single AGWPE connection to an
.BR ax25netd (8)
loop port.  With
.B target tcp
the connection is a TCP socket to
.IR host : tcp-port ,
with
.B target socket
a unix domain socket at
.IR path .
.SH LISTEN
Each
.B listen
line opens one front side listener.  Several are allowed.
.PP
.RS
.B listen tcp
.I address binary-port [ text-port ]
.br
.B listen unix
.I path [ group all|default|name|gid ]
.RE
.PP
.B listen tcp
binds the binary port at
.IR address : binary-port .
The binary port treats everything received after the command line as
one packet: it is accumulated and sent as a single AX.25 frame when the
connection closes, split into
.B mtu
sized chunks.  The text port, by default one number above the binary
port (or at
.I text-port
when given), sends each CR, LF or CRLF terminated line as one frame.
The address
.B 0.0.0.0
listens on all interfaces.
.PP
.B listen unix
listens on a unix domain socket which behaves exactly like a text port.
With
.B group
the socket is restricted to the given group (a name or a numeric gid);
.B all
makes it world accessible, the default gives it to the daemon's user.
.SH MISCELLANEOUS
.PP
.RS
.B mtu
.I bytes
.RE
.PP
The datagram packet chunk size, 16 to 4096 bytes.  The default is 256.
.PP
.RS
.B default-call
.I callsign
.RE
.PP
The source callsign used when a command line does not give one.  Without
it a connect or datagram command must name its source call explicitly.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
	# binary port 8101, text port 8102
	# back side from ax25common.conf (loop socket/tcp)
	listen	tcp	127.0.0.1	8101
	listen	tcp	127.0.0.1	8102
	listen	unix	@@@AX25_LOCALSTATEDIR@@@/ax25/ax25tcpd.sock
	#target	tcp	192.0.2.10	8100
	mtu	256
	default-call	DG8HT
.fi
.SH FILES
.I @@@AX25_SYSCONFDIR@@@/ax25tcpd.conf
.br
.I @@@AX25_SYSCONFDIR@@@/ax25common.conf
(back side unless overridden)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ax25tcpd (8),
.BR ax25netd (8),
.BR ax25common.conf (5),
.BR agwpe.conf (5)
